        26["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Layered World</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Coordinates and key packing<br />(x, y, z), tile rules as data<br />(TILE_INFO), and chunked<br />terrain: the forest surface<br />at z = 0 from noise octaves,<br />solid geology below with one<br />shaft per chunk. Chunks are<br />generated lazily and<br />LRU-cached; player edits<br />(richness mods), per-layer<br />fog and the holes between<br />layers live outside the<br />cache. Explored chunks and<br />observed resource types have<br />derived spatial indexes,<br />including one/two-unit<br />reserve masks that remove<br />exhausted deposits from<br />searches; Map/Set-compatible<br />geometry and prop<br />notifications invalidate<br />dependent light fields and<br />charger candidates.</div>"]
        style 26 fill:#3f7d3a,stroke:#2c5728,color:#ffffff
        28["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Simulation Step</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>step(s, dt): production,<br />logistics, abundance income,<br />battery and the burning<br />flare; movement and fog<br />reveal as far as your light<br />reaches (sightRadius).<br />Browser and AUTO hosts enable<br />cumulative solo production<br />after Logistics: grouped<br />rates, cached counts/mastery,<br />command/query settlements,<br />and buffer snapshots at saves<br />or rate changes. Visual<br />events query nearby tile<br />buckets. Cultivation runs<br />local environment deadlines<br />at 250ms in the same<br />canonical step. Chunk-cached<br />sky/artificial illumination<br />follows rock and open ladder<br />connections; direct sky<br />columns retain strength,<br />diffuse paths attenuate, and<br />local dependency invalidation<br />rebuilds fields from<br />surviving sources. A<br />canonical carried-light<br />selector allows one lantern<br />or flare, shared by commands,<br />battery, rendering and<br />controls; old saves normalize<br />overlaps without losing<br />equipment. Carried fields<br />change only at source<br />tile/strength changes. Sun<br />phases reuse sky access;<br />rendering and proportional<br />crystal exposure consume the<br />same field, with player<br />awareness and remembered<br />exploration separate. Battery<br />intervals support quiet-tick<br />batching and reuse nearby<br />charger candidates with exact<br />range and daylight checks.<br />Reveal compares exact circle<br />row intervals and visits<br />newly covered edges. Resource<br />streams settle together with<br />targeted manual balance<br />updates. Variable-step/shared<br />callers and extreme<br />arithmetic retain the legacy<br />economy.</div>"]
        style 28 fill:#3f7d3a,stroke:#2c5728,color:#ffffff
        29["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Actions</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Harvest (gather deposits on<br />the surface, dig rock<br />underground), Trail sweep<br />targets, collect, and build;<br />plus travel between layers<br />through holes (dig down from<br />the forest, climb up through<br />the ceiling, drop through<br />holes and shafts). All<br />personal world actions share<br />interaction.js: walkable<br />same-layer contact on the<br />object's tile or a cardinal<br />side; no diagonal or distant<br />reach. Collection empties one<br />contacted building.<br />Infrastructure remains<br />independent of player<br />contact.</div>"]
