        12["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Renderer</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Paints all floor tiles before<br />standing objects in<br />north-to-south row order.<br />Physical light shades each<br />device-pixel-aligned terrain<br />face in painter order. Static<br />standing art shares an<br />8M-pixel/128-entry LRU of<br />source-picture and 64 opacity<br />buckets; animated and<br />vector-only objects use a<br />capacity-reused<br />viewport-clipped transparent<br />patch; no flat darkness mask<br />slices raised art. Gameplay<br />terrain stays live; the atlas<br />owns distant map zoom. Local<br />viewport-bounded masks<br />preserve higher foreground<br />terrain occlusion without<br />clipping feet against<br />equal-height floor. The faint<br />visibility pass omits<br />character and boat shadows;<br />placement ghosts share the<br />masks, Wiki focus and map<br />mode retain their independent<br />paths, and renderer fault<br />recovery restores canvas<br />clipping. The default player<br />is Mica, a compact flat<br />orange-hooded repairer with<br />skinned split coat/patch,<br />explicit-time mesh-eye blinks<br />and curious idle/recovery<br />poses, actual-cargo<br />protective carrying and world<br />inspection, with eight<br />snapped world headings:<br />twenty-one bone hierarchy<br />with four weighted cloak<br />panels, one-handed mining<br />from the shaft's end and<br />fixed-length arm IK to the<br />WORK_HANDS targets in<br />work-motion.js, earned<br />palm-bound baskets and belt<br />lanterns from<br />work-equipment.js, free-hand<br />assembly and a one-cycle<br />coalescing actor queue with<br />captured work facing, torso<br />and head counterbalance,<br />articulated elbows and<br />wrists, and pure two-bone leg<br />IK plus layered action curves<br />from rig-motion.js.<br />rig-model.js builds the rig<br />without a renderer and names<br />its solids and their joints<br />and grips; rig-clips.js finds<br />crossing triangles between<br />them, which the unit sweep<br />and the local dev build treat<br />as a fault.<br />rigged-character.js lazily<br />bundles vendored Three.js and<br />reuses one 320x448 WebGL<br />surface composited into the<br />2D canvas. Wiki, a four-bone<br />mycelium sprite with a<br />skinned folding cap<br />(wiki-model.js, pure pose in<br />wiki-motion.js), rides the<br />hood bone in the same pass<br />and outline; src/game/wiki.js<br />decides what it looks at and<br />says (a long press on the map<br />asks it), Mica and Wiki have<br />no pointer hit targets;<br />gestures pass to the world,<br />and focus.js rings what it<br />talks about in Wiki teal<br />around the whole object.<br />pickaxe-model.js supplies<br />cached six-tier palm/back<br />equipment and offline-baked<br />matching icons, one flat fill<br />mesh per tier with no ink<br />shell; the character contour<br />outlines it while equipped<br />and a 2D silhouette stamp<br />outlines the icons.<br />Action/boat feedback shares<br />canonical timing;<br />presentation never runs<br />simulation ticks. Mica is not<br />drawn while the rig loads;<br />without WebGL and for<br />friends, the 2D wanderer<br />stands in. A cached<br />multisampled color target and<br />one alpha-derived<br />screen-space ink pass outline<br />the complete figure,<br />replacing per-piece hulls.<br />Exact sRGB fills are<br />preserved, with no CPU<br />readback in normal rendering.<br />Geometry, combined-pass draw<br />calls and compressed module<br />size are bounded.<br />resource-models.js builds<br />four canonical 3D materials<br />and offline vector views<br />through<br />scripts/resource-art.mjs;<br />icons/deposits/small piles<br />remain cached texture-pack<br />SVGs at runtime, flat value<br />planes over one whole-object<br />ink silhouette with no face<br />or part edges. No player<br />text.</div>"]
        style 12 fill:#b0761f,stroke:#7b5215,color:#ffffff
        5["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Main Loop</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Wires the modules together<br />and owns the current state<br />(game.state, replaced on<br />embark/reset). Schedules the<br />shared fixed-tick engine<br />independently of drawing. All<br />devices target 30 FPS while<br />acting or standing still<br />through a shared strict<br />deadline pacer, which waits<br />near refresh boundaries<br />without drawing early.<br />Bounded diagnostics<br />distinguish whole-loop CPU,<br />outside-loop time, normal cap<br />allowance, excess interval<br />and measured timer lateness;<br />a cheap CPU phase is not<br />claimed to cause a slow<br />frame. Each simulation tick<br />steers, steps the Core,<br />reveals fog, works held input<br />and ticks AUTO; presentation<br />separately updates effects,<br />save/HUD timers and<br />rendering. A frame, a drawing<br />layer or a tap that throws is<br />skipped and kept as a problem<br />report (faults.js,<br />problems.js); only frames<br />failing in a row stop the<br />game. Exposes window.MTE_GAME<br />for the browser tests.</div>"]
